#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-weathervaning.rst:4
#: 787efae2216f4a5993b4484c60bb3f7a
msgid "Weathervaning and Wind Hold"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-weathervaning.rst:6
#: 75c96e3b54674b049019507ea4509d22
msgid "Flying a QuadPlane in significant levels of wind can present a challenge. The issue is that the large wing surface offers a lot of surface area for the wind to interact with. That can lead to a reduction in attitude and position control and high motor and ESC load."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-weathervaning.rst:12
#: 0e6a1667c7d04dcfad2234cdb39c9250
msgid "To reduce the impact of wind when flying in VTOL modes the ArduPilot QuadPlane code supports two features:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-weathervaning.rst:15
#: 56e32b5dffe040a5a61aba60beee877b
msgid "Active yaw axis weathervaning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-weathervaning.rst:16
#: 15f7bc80698b423c970b61ba8b19f0bd
msgid "Position hold assistance using forward or tilt rotor motors instead of only using VTOL stance tilting"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-weathervaning.rst:18
#: f5ad631a88854942b003d42325de40db
msgid "Together these two features can greatly reduce the impact of wind on VTOL flight by keeping the aircraft pointed into the wind and reducing the area of the wing exposed to the wind."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-weathervaning.rst:23
#: 2f972b9cc9204ab6b9edd0c6a8a47cc8
msgid "Active Weathervaning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-weathervaning.rst:25
#: bc13eea88ecc49c99c02fa6db36573b7
msgid "Active weathervaning acts to turn the aircraft into the wind when flying in position-controlled VTOL modes. You can enable active weathervaning by setting the :ref:`Q_WVANE_ENABLE <Q_WVANE_ENABLE>` parameter to a non-zero value. The default is not to use active weathervaning."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-weathervaning.rst:32
#: 6012b36713eb4c4b9ed2b7ffaca1abc9
msgid ":ref:`Q_WVANE_ENABLE<Q_WVANE_ENABLE>` Value"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-weathervaning.rst:32
#: ca679e2c88e34628afca9744fcc2777c
msgid "Weathervane Direction"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-weathervaning.rst:34
#: e01157891a5842d28e2da2762876c790
msgid "0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-weathervaning.rst:34
#: 5262a1af4d3349018333288f6547e732
msgid "Disabled"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-weathervaning.rst:36
#: 7ec6a723717645d8898d34e85aeb126a
msgid "1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-weathervaning.rst:36
#: 8baa8e3ffa3347d1aecbc0f23acfe66a
msgid "Nose Into Wind(default)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-weathervaning.rst:38
#: a5a1d73c215f49fea7651742abef2920
msgid "2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-weathervaning.rst:38
#: 3ccf7d2f9d8a442790537c0772045b10
msgid "Nose OR Tail Into Wind"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-weathervaning.rst:40
#: acaee24f96c947a5a2f32271baabfb69
msgid "3"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-weathervaning.rst:40
#: b0be99aba6424afe9eee5aaf29f55658
msgid "Side Into Wind"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-weathervaning.rst:42
#: fe8cfbdf2d8a438592b1c990d714f6e9
msgid "4"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-weathervaning.rst:42
#: b2421db038d449829fe3d1a2a5846348
msgid "Tail Into Wind"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-weathervaning.rst:45
#: d2b15bc308d7495fb8cadce25c80a7ea
msgid "The way it works is the autopilot looks at the roll and/or pitch attitude needed to control the desired position. The basic algorithm is \"yaw into the roll/pitch\". If the aircraft needs hold roll to the right in order to hold position then it will turn in that direction on the assumption that the right roll is needed in order to hold against the wind (assuming nose into the wind). Similarly, for Side Into the Wind, it will use the pitch angle and yaw appropriately, trying to zero the pitch required to hold position."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-weathervaning.rst:51
#: 3d9c94debed8464db46371d3a6333f17
msgid "by default, weathervaning does not use pitch, only roll. This is to prevent unwanted continuous yawing if the hover attitude has not been trimmed with :ref:`Q_TRIM_PITCH<Q_TRIM_PITCH>` to hover, in place, with no wind. If this **has** been done, then pitch driven weathervaning can be enabled by setting :ref:`Q_WVANE_OPTIONS<Q_WVANE_OPTIONS>` bit 0 to \"1\". This will speed weathervaning if positioned with the wind blowing from behind (ie mostly being held in position with pitch, not roll). This does not affect Side Into Wind, it always uses pitch, and :ref:`Q_TRIM_PITCH<Q_TRIM_PITCH>` must be properly set for good operation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-weathervaning.rst:53
#: ca5d9248cbba4b90a7ee543f374390ee
msgid "How quickly the aircraft yaws is determined by the :ref:`Q_WVANE_GAIN<Q_WVANE_GAIN>` parameter. It converts the lean angle into degs/sec of yaw. A good value to start with is 1 (1 degree roll = 1 deg/sec yaw if :ref:`Q_PLT_Y_RATE<Q_PLT_Y_RATE>` =90). Higher values for gain or rate will make the aircraft turn into the roll more quickly. If the overall correcting yaw rate is too high then you can get instability and oscillation in yaw."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-weathervaning.rst:58
#: 3a44bf8d158540809c7044ac7992f7c6
msgid "To cope with a small amount of trim in the aircraft there is an additional parameter :ref:`Q_WVANE_ANG_MIN<Q_WVANE_ANG_MIN>` which controls the minimum roll/pitch level before weathervaning will be used. This defaults to one degree. If you find your aircraft starts yawing even in no wind then you may need to raise this value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-weathervaning.rst:64
#: f6476e31cb814f30a82c53d497daf952
msgid "Active weathervaning is only active in VTOL modes, and VTOL sections of AUTO modes (such as VTOL takeoff and VTOL landing). It is not active in QSTABILIZE and QHOVER modes as those are not position controlled modes. It is active is QLOITER, QLAND and QRTL modes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-weathervaning.rst:69
#: 6a9fe99dcacc4ae49c7cde3d115d454f
msgid "There are a number of additional parameters that can control when WeatherVaning is active (all are disabled by default):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-weathervaning.rst:71
#: f2bdb643b4a446b39c0aeb242fc438a9
msgid ":ref:`Q_WVANE_HGT_MIN<Q_WVANE_HGT_MIN>`: above this height weathervaning is permitted"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-weathervaning.rst:72
#: 0fa2e164a1e3416fafa84d852162709d
msgid ":ref:`Q_WVANE_SPD_MAX<Q_WVANE_SPD_MAX>`: below this ground speed weathervaning is permitted"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-weathervaning.rst:73
#: 19117ca52a8a48c981b6df4bd21b6763
msgid ":ref:`Q_WVANE_VELZ_MAX<Q_WVANE_VELZ_MAX>`: maximum climb or descent speed at which the vehicle will still attempt to weathervane"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-weathervaning.rst:74
#: aa16efb87ef0494da34c8cb07ce17083
msgid ":ref:`Q_WVANE_TAKEOFF<Q_WVANE_TAKEOFF>`: override weathervaning direction in auto takeoffs*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-weathervaning.rst:75
#: a9a16b72e0814eb7b896a2b9aed87079
msgid ":ref:`Q_WVANE_LAND<Q_WVANE_LAND>`: override weathervaning directions in auto landings*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-weathervaning.rst:77
#: b769490da49f4685bd1bfc228a4aa106
msgid "note:* not QLOITER take-offs and landings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-weathervaning.rst:79
#: d3eaf37125ad4a84bd596dad763005e2
msgid "Weathervaning can be disabled or enabled by an :ref:`RC Aux Function Switch<common-auxiliary-functions>`, option \"160\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-weathervaning.rst:82
#: 509ad127dfbb4636bb7fb15b840e4250
msgid "Using the Forward or Tilt Motors to Help Position Holding"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-weathervaning.rst:84
#: 946a49b25c314a78a4906ac4fbea22d0
msgid "In addition to active weathervaning, the QuadPlane code supports using the forward motor or tilting the tilt rotors to hold the pitch level in VTOL flight modes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-weathervaning.rst:87
#: e543d7986a8f4944b5b2d4fb1e4664eb
msgid "In firmware versions prior to 4.5, to enable use of the forward motor(s)/tilting motors for position hold you need to set the :ref:`Q_VFWD_GAIN <Q_VFWD_GAIN>` parameter to a non-zero value. This will be active in QLOITER, QRTL, QLAND and in AUTO mode when executing VTOL flight commands.This method uses the velocity controller."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-weathervaning.rst:90
#: 6d4ffc63fae54aadbe4071bfbbfa20e8
msgid "In firmware versions 4.5 and later, use of this mechanism is no longer recommended and has been superseded by a new method which reduces the pitch forward experienced with the method activated using non-zero :ref:`Q_VFWD_GAIN <Q_VFWD_GAIN>`. This method is enabled by setting :ref:`Q_FWD_THR_GAIN<Q_FWD_THR_GAIN>` and :ref:`Q_FWD_THR_USE<Q_FWD_THR_USE>` to non-zero values. This newer method uses the position controller to control the forward motor/tilt."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-weathervaning.rst:93
#: 9a94762f570444a4bb23ef8fc11b6a22
msgid "Tailsitters do not have these options and :ref:`Q_VFWD_GAIN <Q_VFWD_GAIN>`, :ref:`Q_FWD_THR_GAIN<Q_FWD_THR_GAIN>` or :ref:`Q_FWD_THR_USE<Q_FWD_THR_USE>`, should be kept at the default value of 0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-weathervaning.rst:96
#: 719b911341bd4307bed93ab18a9be6eb
msgid "Old Method (Q_VFWD_GAIN)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-weathervaning.rst:98
#: e30ec7b885ee4b74b47ec8b2e2033b75
msgid "The way it works is to look at two factors:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-weathervaning.rst:100
#: 035dd648b1474effa913bb855b7abd33
msgid "the navigation attitude pitch of the aircraft (which can be up to :ref:`Q_A_ANGLE_MAX<Q_A_ANGLE_MAX>`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-weathervaning.rst:101
#: 588821f01def4ff593b4dfe8aec7f487
msgid "the difference between the desired forward velocity and the actual forward velocity"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-weathervaning.rst:104
#: df5c0bb61332422cb6a28de45d293773
msgid "These are combined with the :ref:`Q_VFWD_GAIN<Q_VFWD_GAIN>` to ramp up and down the throttle on the forward motor in order to minimize the attitude pitch of the aircraft. That keeps the area of wing exposed to the wind minimized which can reduce VTOL motor load."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-weathervaning.rst:109
#: a8bf01dcbf8a47dc96bfe0a40caa3105
msgid "A good value to start with for :ref:`Q_VFWD_GAIN<Q_VFWD_GAIN>` is 0.05. Higher values will use the forward motor more aggressively. If the value is too high you can get severe pitch oscillations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-weathervaning.rst:113
#: 71a41360c8ce439ea8b9717c8398bb2e
msgid "As with active weathervaning, using the forward motor is only enabled in position controlled VTOL modes. This means it is not enabled in QSTABILIZE or QHOVER flight modes. It is available in QLOITER, QRTL, QLAND and in AUTO mode when executing VTOL flight commands."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-weathervaning.rst:119
#: a1c709eefe9e42b38345372200afc108
msgid "New Method (Q_FWD_THR_GAIN)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-weathervaning.rst:121
#: 428948f227554c4caac950175b7dfbb7
msgid "This method uses the position controller to control the forward motor thrust in combination with the navigation pitch angle which can be limited by the :ref:`Q_FWD_PIT_LIM<Q_FWD_PIT_LIM>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-weathervaning.rst:123
#: 3557ae02cc0d41b6a892352b96e8d586
msgid "The :ref:`Q_FWD_THR_GAIN<Q_FWD_THR_GAIN>` parameter sets the gain from forward accel/tilt to forward throttle in Q modes. The Q modes this feature operates in is controlled by the :ref:`Q_FWD_THR_USE<Q_FWD_THR_USE>` parameter. Vehicles using separate forward thrust motors, eg quadplanes, should set this parameter to (all up weight) / (maximum combined thrust of forward motors) with a value of 2 being typical. Vehicles that tilt lifting rotors to provide forward thrust should set this parameter to (all up weight) / (weight lifted by tilting rotors) which for most aircraft can be approximated as (total number of lifting rotors) / (number of lifting rotors that tilt). When using this method of forward throttle control, the forward tilt angle limit is controlled by the :ref:`Q_FWD_PIT_LIM<Q_FWD_PIT_LIM>` parameter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-weathervaning.rst:125
#: 86fe19bc12e54d17b5bc03e591327429
msgid "this use of forward motor can be disabled using an RC switch whose ``RCx_OPTIONS`` param has been set to \"176\" and the switch is moved to mid or low position."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-weathervaning.rst:127
#: 3469cc446ba84a6299fb3bc5159ef5fb
msgid ":ref:`Q_VFWD_ALT<Q_VFWD_ALT>`: when below this relative to home altitude, forward motor assist is disabled. This can be useful to keep the motor propeller from hitting the ground. Rangefinder height data is used when available."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-weathervaning.rst:130
#: af861ce980c640efa53ce5f37d0628da
msgid "Continuous tilt-rotor QuadPlanes will tilt motors up to :ref:`TRIM_THROTTLE<TRIM_THROTTLE>` times :ref:`Q_TILT_MAX<Q_TILT_MAX>` to maintain position."
msgstr ""
